## Terminology

### Core Concepts
- **CAP (Record)**: A "CAP" is Accela's term for a Record. It represents any type of case, application, permit, or project in the system
  - `capID`: The internal unique identifier for a record
  - `customID`: The user-friendly record ID displayed to end users (often called "record ID" in messages)
  - `capModel`: The full data model containing all record information
  - `capClass`: Classification of the record (e.g., Complete, Incomplete)
  - `capStatus`: Current status of the record
  - `fileDate`: Date the record was created

### Record Types
- **CapType (Record Type)**: Defines the type/category of a record. Has 4 components:
  - `group`: High level grouping (e.g., Licenses, Permits)
  - `type`: Main type within the group
  - `subtype`: Further classification
  - `category`: Final level of classification
  - `capTypeString`: Human-readable name for the record type

### Time Accounting
- **TimeLog**: Tracks time spent on activities
  - `timeLogModel`: Contains details about time entries
  - `timeGroupSeq`: Groups related time entries
  - `timeTypeSeq`: Identifies the type of time being logged
  - `billable`: Indicates if time can be billed
  - `totalMinutes`: Duration of the time entry
  - `materials`: Materials used during the activity
  - `mileage`: Distance traveled (start, end, total)

### Record Relationships
- **Project**: A parent record that can have child records
  - Child records can be linked through various relationships
  - Common relationships: Amendment, Renewal, Associated Forms
- **Partial Records**: Incomplete/temporary records often used in online applications
  - Can be converted to regular records later

### Common Terms
- **ServiceProviderCode**: Agency code that identifies which agency/tenant the operation applies to
- **AuditID**: Identifier for who performed an action (usually a user ID)
- **ScriptResult**: Standard return type for EMSE API calls containing:
  - Success/failure status
  - Output data
  - Error messages if applicable
- **ACA**: Accela Citizen Access (public web portal)
- **EMSE**: Event Manager Script Engine

### Record Components
- **ASI (Application Specific Info)**: Custom fields on a record
  - Can be grouped into ASI Groups
  - Supports various field types including checkboxes
- **APO (Address/Parcel/Owner)**: Core components of a record
  - Address information
  - Parcel data
  - Owner details
- **Comments**: Notes attached to records
  - Can be attached to specific items (e.g., guide items)
  - Include creation and update tracking
- **Documents**: Files attached to records
- **Contacts**: People or organizations associated with records
- **WorkDesc**: Work description text for the record
